The system must store or display video content only when it has the appropriate rights and permissions.

# 13. Security and Privacy Requirements

1. All production backend communication must use HTTPS.
2. AI-provider API keys must remain on the backend.
3. Secrets must be stored in a secret manager or protected environment configuration.
4. Authentication tokens must be stored using appropriate platform security mechanisms.
5. API endpoints must validate input and enforce rate limits.
6. Sensitive information must not be written to logs unnecessarily.
7. Microphone access must be permission-based and transparent.
8. Recording must stop when the user cancels or the active recording session ends.
9. Users must be informed when audio is processed by an external service.
10. The application must not collect contacts, SMS, private messages, or call history without a legitimate, separately authorized feature.
11. Production error messages must not reveal API keys, stack traces, or private user information.
12. Stored user data must have a documented retention policy.
13. Account deletion and history deletion must be implemented correctly if those features are offered.
14. Third-party integrations must comply with the applicable platform terms and privacy requirements.

# 14. Error Handling

The application must handle these scenarios:

| Scenario | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| Microphone permission denied | Explain the permission requirement and offer text input |
| Speech recognition unavailable | Offer text input or another supported recognition method |
| No speech detected | Ask the user to try again without repeatedly interrupting |
| AI backend unavailable | Display a retry option and preserve the user's typed question when appropriate |
| AI provider error | Show a clear failure message without fabricating an answer |
| Internet unavailable | Allow supported offline UI and local app-launching functions |
| Requested app not installed | Explain that the application is unavailable |
| App launch fails | Report that the launch failed rather than claiming success |
| Unsupported Instagram API access | Explain the limitation and offer the supported feed or external-app option |
| Invalid command | Ask for clarification or explain the supported command |
| User cancels | Stop the current supported operation |
| Voice output disabled | Display the answer as text |
| Session expires | Request authentication again when required |

# 15. Performance Requirements

The following are proposed MVP targets and must be verified through testing:

- App launch to usable Home screen: target under 3 seconds on a supported mid-range device.
- Local application-launch commands: initiate the launch promptly after recognition.
- Backend response time: target a typical AI response within 5 seconds when the provider and network allow it.
- UI interactions: remain responsive while network requests run.
- Video playback: avoid blocking the main UI thread.
- Failed network requests: support reasonable timeouts and user-initiated retries.

AI response times, speech-recognition quality, and video playback performance depend on device hardware, network conditions, and external services.

# 16. Accessibility Requirements

- Provide readable text and sufficient contrast.
- Use accessible labels for interactive elements.
- Do not rely exclusively on color to communicate state.
- Support Android font scaling.
- Provide text alternatives for voice-only interactions.
- Ensure microphone state is visually clear.
- Provide a way to stop speech output.
- Make core navigation usable without voice interaction.

# 17. Analytics and Success Metrics

Analytics must be privacy-conscious and must not record raw microphone audio or full conversation content by default.

Potential product metrics include:

- Number of successful onboarding completions.
- Percentage of voice requests recognized successfully.
- Application-launch success rate.
- AI request success rate.
- Median AI response time.
- Study Mode usage.
- Video-feed playback success rate.
- User-reported crashes and errors.
- Retention and user satisfaction, where measurement is appropriately consented.

The team must define baselines and targets after initial usability testing. These metrics must not be presented as achieved results before actual measurement.

# 18. Testing Requirements

## 18.1 Unit Testing

Test:

- Command classification.
- Language selection.
- Request validation.
- Backend error handling.
- Settings persistence.
- Permission-state handling.

## 18.2 Integration Testing

Test:

- Android client to backend communication.
- Backend to configured AI provider.
- Speech recognition to command router.
- Command router to Android app launching.
- Text-to-speech start and stop behavior.
- Authorized video-feed data retrieval.

## 18.3 Device Testing

Test on supported Android versions and multiple screen sizes.

Include devices with:

- Instagram installed.
- Instagram not installed.
- WhatsApp installed.
- WhatsApp not installed.
- Microphone permission denied.
- Internet unavailable.
- Speech recognition unavailable.
- Voice output disabled.

## 18.4 Privacy and Security Testing

Verify:

- API keys are not present in the APK.
- Unauthorized users cannot retrieve other users' histories.
- Microphone use follows permission and disclosure requirements.
- User cancellation stops recording and speech output.
- Network errors do not expose private information.
- History deletion works when history storage is enabled.

## 18.5 Acceptance Tests

The MVP will be accepted only when:

1. The app installs and launches on a supported Android device.
2. The Home screen and settings work.
3. A user can type a question and receive an AI answer when the backend is configured.
4. A user can activate voice input and submit a recognized question.
5. A greeting produces one short response and then waits.
6. The assistant does not initiate unsolicited speech.
7. The assistant follows the configured voice-output setting.
8. The assistant responds in a supported language appropriate to the user's request.
9. A supported command launches the actual installed application.
10. An unavailable application produces a clear error.
11. The app never falsely reports an unconfirmed action as successful.
12. Study Mode can answer supported educational questions.
13. Permission denial and network failures are handled safely.
14. No fake Instagram or WhatsApp integration is presented as real.
15. The video feed is accepted only if its selected content source and playback functionality are genuinely implemented.

